      "internal": false,
      "mergeID": "6639b15c16e7e5fc77513539",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Now that moderated Group+ and Group Public instances are a thing, the ability to warn, kick, and ban people from world instances has been opened up to a lot more people. \n\nA problem has arisen, however, that there is no way to provide a reason that will be communicated to that user in any way. \n\nThis has caused huge misinterpretations over the reason people get kicked or banned for, and in some extreme cases has led to people going around other instances trying to spread rumors and slander the group owners and moderators over what they feel was being unfairly punished.\n\nA text field on the prompt that lets you (optionally) type a message, which would then show to the user after they have been moderated, would help a lot. \n\nFor example, someone seeing \"You were kicked because your music was too loud\" or \"You were kicked for lagging the whole instance\", or \"You have been warned for disrupting our stream\", would avoid a lot of these scenarios.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Allow specifying a reason for Group Instance Kicks/Bans/Warns",
      "pinned": false,
      "postID": "64c7f1ccebc3952f0ed5fa3b",
